    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required validating an E.164 telephone's national-number length per country code (`+61` \u2192 9 national digits, `+1` \u2192 10), rejecting with 400 otherwise. The existing `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` only enforced a global 8\u201315 digit range, which doesn't distinguish per country.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I **added behaviour as a new small unit** rather than growing the existing normalize method:\n\n- **New `ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`** \u2014 a fresh class (WMC_other \u2248 0), one public `service` method (CC 1, straight-line) delegating to a tiny private `check` helper (CC 2). It runs after normalization, so it works on the already-formed E.164 value.\n- **Wired one `countryLength` step** into `owners.POST.yml` between `normalize` and `email`.\n\nTwo files touched, and no existing function's complexity was increased. The valid owner payload (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 9 national digits after dropping the leading `0`) still passes; `+61 123` now rejects with 400.",
